  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the species <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>BH</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>. Choose the correct option with respect to the there species:<br />&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "They are isoelectronic and only two have tetrahedral structures<br />&nbsp;",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "They are isoelectronic and all have tetrahedral structures<br />&nbsp;",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Only two are isoelectronic and all have tetrahedral structures<br />&nbsp;",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Only two are isoelectronic and only two have tetrahedral structures",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>In</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><msub><mi>BH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo></math>the number of electrons are 10 for each.</p><p>Hence, all the three species given are isoelectronic, and the central atom shows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridization. Hence, they have tetrahedral structure.</p>"
  }
